line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">A deliberately elementary model of a square-zero differential, indexed by natural numbers.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">namespace</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Fixture2000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/-- **Definition 1** (Fixture2000). A natural-number-indexed toy chain complex. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">structure</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> ChainComplexToy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> where</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">  /-- The distinguished degree. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  degree : Nat</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">  /-- The differential at each degree. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  differential : Nat → Nat → Nat</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">  /-- Each differential preserves zero. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  differential_zero : ∀ n, differential n </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">  /-- Consecutive differentials compose to zero. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  square_zero : ∀ n x, differential n (differential (n + </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) x) = </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">end</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Fixture2000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>",
    "source_text": "/-!\n```yaml node\n{\n  \"id\": \"Fixture2000.Def_1\",\n  \"kind\": \"definition\",\n  \"doc\": \"Fixture2000\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"chapter\": \"1\",\n    \"section\": \"1.1\",\n    \"label\": \"Definition 1\",\n    \"pages\": [\n      1\n    ]\n  },\n  \"title\": \"Definition 1\",\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"chain-complex\",\n    \"basic\"\n  ],\n  \"concepts\": {\n    \"defines\": [\n      \"chain-complex\"\n    ],\n    \"uses\": []\n  },\n  \"deps\": {\n    \"statement\": [],\n    \"proof\": []\n  },\n  \"decls\": [\n    \"Fixture2000.ChainComplexToy\"\n  ],\n  \"fidelity\": {\n    \"status\": \"faithful\"\n  },\n  \"mathlib\": {\n    \"relation\": \"variant\",\n    \"decls\": [\n      \"Function.comp\"\n    ],\n    \"bridge\": \"Fixture2000.Bridge_Def_1_mathlib\",\n    \"note\": \"The square-zero law can equivalently be expressed using function composition; this toy complex is not an alias for a Mathlib complex.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Statement\n\nA toy chain complex consists of a natural number called its degree and a family of functions $d_n : \\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N}$ such that $d_n(0)=0$ and $d_n(d_{n+1}(x))=0$ for every $n,x \\in \\mathbb{N}$.\n\n## Description\n\nA deliberately elementary model of a square-zero differential, indexed by natural numbers.\n-/\n\nnamespace Fixture2000\n\n/-- **Definition 1** (Fixture2000). A natural-number-indexed toy chain complex. -/\nstructure ChainComplexToy where\n  /-- The distinguished degree. -/\n  degree : Nat\n  /-- The differential at each degree. -/\n  differential : Nat → Nat → Nat\n  /-- Each differential preserves zero. -/\n  differential_zero : ∀ n, differential n 0 = 0\n  /-- Consecutive differentials compose to zero. -/\n  square_zero : ∀ n x, differential n (differential (n + 1) x) = 0\n\nend Fixture2000\n"
  },
